If you were creating a Fabric Git Integration persona framework for design discussions, I would group them into 3 macro-personas:
Persona	GoalCreator (BI Dev, Data Engineer, Data Scientist)	Build and version Fabric assets
Collaborator (Professional Developer, Team Lead)	Review, merge, and coordinate changes
Operator (Admin, DevOps, Platform Owner)	Govern, automate, and deploy safely

This Creator → Collaborator → Operator model is the simplest way to explain who Git Integration is for and why each group cares about it.
